  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Mainly dry uneventful weather expected today through \nTuesday.\n\nA cool advection will continue with 850 mb temps getting down \naround +9C. With lake temps still sitting around +22/+23C, this \nwill be enough to elicit a weak lake response. A NNE cross-lake \nflow over Lake Ontario will produce some lake clouds south of \nthat lake, and with an added boost from upslope flow, there will\nalso be a few light lake enhanced showers...with the best \nchances for these found across the Finger Lakes region through \nearly this morning.\n\nOtherwise...surface high pressure over the upper Great Lakes builds \nsouth into the lower Great Lakes region today and into Labor Day. \nThis will end any shower potential with dry weather expected through \nMonday, and even through the day Tuesday. \n\nWe will also see a gradual warming trend as we work through the \nfirst half of the upcoming week. \n\nThe next chance for showers and thunderstorms will potentially \narrive Wednesday as a low moves east across Ontario and Quebec\nwhile sending its trailing cold front across the Great Lakes.",
